# Origin: legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/date.chk
# Milestone: M6 Wave 2 (Phase 11 partial port)
#
# Legacy fixture exercises `Date.epoch - Date.epoch + 9220000`, an
# arithmetic seam over a Date "epoch zero" instance.  v0.6.1 has no
# Date.epoch slot; the equivalent semantic check is to construct a
# Date directly from a seconds offset and read .seconds() back.
#
# Wave-2 deferred (full port): Date.epoch constant slot, Date `-`
# returning a Duration, Date `+` Integer, Date arithmetic operator
# overrides via .u overlay (Phase 10 finding #4 — operator-via-slot-
# install doesn't intercept inline VM opcodes yet).  See PORT_NOTES.md.

Date.fromSeconds(9220000).seconds()
[00000000] 9220000

Date.fromSeconds(9230000).seconds()
[00000001] 9230000

Date.fromSeconds(0).seconds()
[00000002] 0

Date.fromSeconds(0).asString()
[00000003] "1970-01-01 00:00:00"

# Date.now() returns a Date with non-zero seconds (post-epoch).
Date.now().seconds() > 0
[00000004] true
